      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 00 -- oh, pardon me -- 01-332, the Board of Education of Independent School District No. 92 of Pottawatomie County v. Lindsay Earls."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Board of Education of Independent School District No. 92 of Pottawatomie County (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves the constitutionality of the Tecumseh School Board's decision to implement a suspicionless drug testing policy for students in competitive activities as a reasonable response to student drug use."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, this policy goes beyond what was permitted in Vernonia, does it not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court record",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "among the -- the class of people subject to this challenge, there have been only three instances of any drug use found."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Meoli (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The purpose of this program is not to discipline students. It's not to catch them. It is to deter drug use and to help those students --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A school district that reasonably concludes that it faces a drug problem may adopt random drug tests for students engaged in competitive extracurricular activities without violating the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Suppose you've had hard statistical evidence to show that the kids that go out for the extracurricular activities are the ones that really do not use drugs, that the high drug user population is in those that don't engage in the activities. What -- what would your recommendation be to the school board at that point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But if -- if that is the case, what is the danger in the school case, comparable to the -- to the railroad worker's danger or the -- the customs officer's danger? What is the danger as distinct from simply the desire to deter illegal drug use?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Opposing counsel said we have to draw the line somewhere, and the -- the way to draw the line in this case is to keep in mind the core principle that individualized reasonable suspicion is the standard for school searches set forth in T.L.O."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOYD: Throat swabs if you think there's a contagious disease. I'm not --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "cameras in the halls, security guards, drug dogs that sweep through the school and the -- and the parking lot and the students. They search lockers. They have teachers who are trained in looking for drug use."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Yes, but they have a record here that, of course, suggests if you want to know if drugs are going on in your school, you ask the kids."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "School",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They say on page 192, minimal problems have been experienced due to violent safety and discipline problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jean Burkett",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the brief by the parents, the amicus brief -- Jean Burkett is the lead one -- really engages this question in a very vigorous and intelligent manner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Boyd",
      "case_id": "2001-01-332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a690d7bb2f382b89be27d86224df3399e02a28b9a6f391ce9896a2dac0b004f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a690d7bb2f38-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOYD: Death from overdose is certainly a concern, but there's no --"
    },
